title: DarkBlinders RuntimeBroker Backdoor Execution from LocalAppData
id: 23826c31-5b0c-4498-ac86-5114c8675d4a
status: experimental
description: >
    Detects the DarkBlinders (UNC5795) AppDomainManager backdoor described by
    Dream Research Labs: a legitimate signed vshost.exe renamed RuntimeBroker.exe
    is dropped under %LOCALAPPDATA%\Microsoft\RuntimeBroker together with
    RuntimeBroker.dll and RuntimeBrokerApi.dll. Any process launched from that
    user-writable directory is anomalous, because the genuine Windows
    RuntimeBroker executes from System32.
references:
    - https://dreamgroup.com/blog/darkblinders-inside-an-active-espionage-campaign
    - https://thehackernews.com/2026/11/darkblinders-compromises-israeli-target.html
    - https://gbhackers.com/darkblinders-hackers-use-fake-meeting-app/
author: Tia N. List
date: 2026/11/03
tags:
    - attack.t1036
    - attack.t1547
    - attack.t1102
    - attack.t1059
    - attack.t1027
logsource:
    category: process_creation
    product: windows
detection:
    selection_image_path:
        Image|contains:
            - '\AppData\Local\Microsoft\RuntimeBroker\'
    selection_backdoor_module:
        CommandLine|contains:
            - 'RuntimeBrokerApi.dll'
            - 'PsProxy.dll'
    condition: selection_image_path or selection_backdoor_module
falsepositives:
    - Unknown; the genuine RuntimeBroker.exe runs from C:\Windows\System32, not LocalAppData
level: high
